# Text checks out with LF on every OS. Windows runners default to core.autocrlf=true, which turned every golden
# (telemetry, cli, resources, runtime, tui) into CRLF there, so byte-for-byte comparisons failed on Windows only.
* text=auto eol=lf
# Windows batch files stay as committed (CRLF), byte for byte.
*.bat -text
*.cmd -text
